language 0.1.0
module localization
  means
    Adaptation of the presentation of content and values to the linguistic and
    regional expectations of a user, leaving the original meaning unchanged.

entity locale : thing
  means
    locale: a named set of linguistic, regional and formatting rules applied
    when presenting information to a user.

entity language : thing
  means
    language: a natural language in which content is created or provided to a
    user.

entity region : thing
  means
    region: a geographic or administrative area determining the applicable
    regional conventions.

entity translation : thing
  means
    translation: localised content conveying the meaning of the original
    content in another language.

entity translatable-unit : thing
  means
    translatable unit: the smallest identifiable fragment of content for which
    a translation is chosen independently.

entity format-rule : thing
  means
    format rule: a rule for presenting a typed value in accordance with a
    locale.

entity time-zone : thing
  means
    time zone: the rules mapping moments in time to local date and time for a
    definite area.

entity currency-format : thing
  means
    currency format: a rule for presenting a monetary value and the
    designation of its currency in accordance with a locale.

entity fallback : thing
  means
    fallback: a rule for choosing another locale or language when the required
    localised content is absent.
